          },
          "hints": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "After the equivalence point, all of the HClO has been neutralized. The amount of titrant (OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ") added after the equivalence point will be used to calculate the pH. Note that the ClO"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " produced in the titration will undergo a base-dissociation reaction, but the OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " produced by this reaction is insignificant compared to the OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " added after the equivalence point."
                    }
                  ],
